[COMMENTS]
STATION,Trapezoidal flume with side contractions. IH/UKCEH experimental catchment. Responsive natural flow regime. GENERAL: A compound sharp-edged weir, capacity 10 cumecs, with flanking broad crests 1953-1958. Trapezoidal flume with side contractions since 1968, capacity 43 cumecs. 15 min. runoff totals available, also rainfall, evaporation and soil data from a dense monitoring network. STATION HYDROMETRY: Flat recessions and flow jumps related to silting/flushing of the flume/inlet pipe. U/s silt trap (installed 1971) improved station performance but sensitivity a limiting factor at lowest flows. Three peak flow ratings applied across period of record, the most recent is valid from February 1971. FLOW RECORD: Poor quality data from 1953-58 (some notable minima, e.g. summer 1955). Record gaps not recoverable. Aug 1976 flows considered the lowest on record. Aug 1977 peak due to very intense local storm (90mm in 2 hrs); little impact in neighbouring catchment (55008). Daily mean flows and AMAX series replaced from 01/10/1973 - 31/12/2010 following detailed QC (August 2025, WINFAP Files v14). Flows 1971-1973 quality controlled visually independently of later (post 1973) flows; 15 minute flow data considered broadly consistent with NRFA daily and peak flows, May-July 1973 removed as likely erroneous. FLOW REGIME: Responsive natural flow regime.
CATCHMENT,High relief, very wet catchment developed on Palaeozoic shales, grits and mudstones. Forest slopes very steep, peat moorland hilltops. Around 2/3 of catchment afforested up to 1985 when some clear felling took place.
Qmed Suitability,Although no gauging information, weir equations expected to perform well. Suitable post 1971.
Pooling Suitability,Although no gauging information, weir equations expected to perform well. Suitable post 1971.
[END]
